Third-party material

Open CASCADE Technology (https://dev.opencascade.org) is the geometry kernel. It is licensed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 with the Open CASCADE exception. ShapeCraft links it dynamically and
does not modify it: the release packages carry its libraries unchanged, together with its licence text, and
you may replace those libraries with your own build of the same version. Its source is available from the
address above. Only the crates/kernel-occt crate (a C++ shim plus FFI) touches it; the rest of ShapeCraft
reaches geometry through the kernel-neutral traits in crates/kernel.

Software dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock, each under its own licence.

Icons are drawn in code. Every file asset (images, fonts, materials) is listed with its author, source and
licence in ATTRIBUTION.md.

File formats are implemented from public specifications and from files ShapeCraft's contributors made
themselves: STEP and IGES through Open CASCADE, Parasolid XT from the vendor's published "Parasolid XT
Format Reference", DWG from the Open Design Alliance's published specification, and the .shapr project
format for interoperability only. No vendor code, SDK or library is included or linked.

